Here is the semantic interpretation of the scene based on the provided ontology:

---

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FoggyUrbanDrivingWithTraffic" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :foggyCondition ;
    :hasObstacle :vehicleObstacle1, :vehicleObstacle2 ;
    :hasRisk :occlusionRisk1, :rearEndCollisionRisk1 ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 .

:foggyCondition a :FoggyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy fog reducing visibility on urban road" .

:vehicleObstacle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow taxi in front lane, partially obscured by fog" .

:vehicleObstacle2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow taxi in adjacent lane, partially obscured by fog" .

:evidence1 a :RollingBallIndicator ;
    :description "Fog causing rolling ball effect (motion blur of vehicles)" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :occlusionRisk1, :rearEndCollisionRisk1 .

:occlusionRisk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Heavy fog obscures visibility of vehicles ahead, increasing collision risk" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:rearEndCollisionRisk1 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of rear-end collision due to reduced visibility and braking distance" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .
```

